  _id: 01Page_02-ThomasEdisonLife
  _middleImage: {fileID: 21300000, guid: db8c88c45bbb8a64aaee08c84f8ced11, type: 3}
  _descriptionTitle: 'Menlo Park: the first invention factory'
  _description: "At 29, he built Menlo Park in New Jersey \u2014 the world's first
    R&D lab \u2014 with a team of 20 engineers. His motto was: \"An invention every
    10 days.\"In 1877 he invented the phonograph, first to record and play sound.
    People thought it was magic.In 1879 he perfected the light bulb with a bamboo
    filament that lasted 1,200 hours, and by 1882 lit up Manhattan. He ended with
    1,093 US patents."
